window.STUDY_PAPERS = {"version":1,"papers":[{"id":"mock-1","title":"模拟卷一","subtitle":"步行 · 外语学习 · 手机使用","description":"根据你提供的参考卷整理，保留原题顺序和选项。","sourceNote":"题目来自继教航标模拟试题（一），答案为逐题核对的参考答案，非出题方公布答案。存疑选择题需对照解析自评。","sourceFiles":"1.png至7.png（共7张）","references":[{"title":"[1] Cambridge Dictionary / All right","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/dictionary/english/all-right"},{"title":"[2] Cambridge Grammar / Why（Why not可表示同意）","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/grammar/british-grammar/why"}],"minutes":120,"questions":[{"number":1,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Excuse me, could you tell me how to get to the City Library from here?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Go straight for two blocks, then turn left. You'll see it."},{"key":"B","text":"Sorry, I don't know the city very well."},{"key":"C","text":"Yes, the library is my favorite place."},{"key":"D","text":"You should ask someone else."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"问路线，A直接给出走法。B表示不熟悉城市，在真实对话中也合理；此处按“提供路线”的命题意图拟选A。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第1题"},{"number":2,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Thanks a lot for helping me with the moving yesterday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"With pleasure."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"C","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"用于回应感谢，意为“不客气”。C的That's all right也可回应感谢，不能把C说成语法或用法错误。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第2题"},{"number":3,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I'm sorry I'm late. I missed the bus.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"That's all right."},{"key":"B","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"C","text":"It was my fault."},{"key":"D","text":"Be careful next time."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方为迟到道歉，回答“没关系”。You're welcome通常回应感谢。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第3题"},{"number":4,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Would you like to join us for dinner this Saturday evening?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I'd love to. What time?"},{"key":"B","text":"You are so kind."},{"key":"C","text":"Let's see."},{"key":"D","text":"Don't bother me."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"接受周六晚餐邀请，并追问时间，前后衔接最完整。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第4题"},{"number":5,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Could you do me a favor and post this letter for me?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"B","text":"No problem."},{"key":"C","text":"Why not?"},{"key":"D","text":"I'm sorry, I'm busy now."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"按答应帮忙拟选B。C的Why not?可表示同意，D则是合理的礼貌拒绝；原题没有限定必须接受请求。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第5题"},{"number":6,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"What do you think of the new movie we saw last night?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I think it's wonderful. The story is touching."},{"key":"B","text":"Let's go and see it again."},{"key":"C","text":"I went there with my friends."},{"key":"D","text":"Yes, I do."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"What do you think of...?询问评价，A直接评价电影和情节。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第6题"},{"number":7,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I just got promoted.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You deserve it."},{"key":"B","text":"Don't mention it."},{"key":"C","text":"It's my pleasure."},{"key":"D","text":"Congratulations!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"听到升职消息，最直接的祝贺是D。A的You deserve it也自然，意为“这是你应得的”。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第7题"},{"number":8,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I failed the driving test again. I feel terrible.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Cheer up! You can try again next time."},{"key":"B","text":"Sorry to hear that."},{"key":"C","text":"You'd better not drive."},{"key":"D","text":"That's terrible news."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"A既安慰又鼓励再试；B的Sorry to hear that也能表达同情，原题存在其他合适回应。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第8题"},{"number":9,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Would you mind if I open the window? It's a bit warm here.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all. Please go ahead."},{"key":"B","text":"Yes, please."},{"key":"C","text":"I don't know."},{"key":"D","text":"It doesn't matter."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"问“介意我开窗吗”，回答“一点也不介意，请开吧”，意思清楚。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第9题"},{"number":10,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I have to leave now. Goodbye.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"See you later."},{"key":"B","text":"How do you do?"},{"key":"C","text":"Good luck."},{"key":"D","text":"Take it easy."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方告别，用“回头见”回应。How do you do用于初次见面。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第10题"},{"number":11,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He is ______ of heights and refuses to climb the mountain.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"afraid"},{"key":"B","text":"afraiding"},{"key":"C","text":"affray"},{"key":"D","text":"afford"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"be afraid of表示“害怕”。后文拒绝爬山，与怕高相符。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第11题"},{"number":12,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"If you don't understand the meaning of this word, please ______ the word in the dictionary.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"look up"},{"key":"B","text":"look over"},{"key":"C","text":"look for"},{"key":"D","text":"look into"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"look up a word in a dictionary表示“在词典里查词”。look for是寻找。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第12题"},{"number":13,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"She ______ her coffee before going to work every morning when she lived in London.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is used to drink"},{"key":"B","text":"used to drink"},{"key":"C","text":"used to drinking"},{"key":"D","text":"uses to drink"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"when she lived in London指过去；used to do表示过去的习惯。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第13题"},{"number":14,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Although he is poor, he is still ______ of his children's education.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pride"},{"key":"B","text":"proud"},{"key":"C","text":"proudful"},{"key":"D","text":"proudly"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"be proud of表示“为……感到自豪”。pride是名词，proudly是副词。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第14题"},{"number":15,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You should ______ your attention to your study instead of playing games.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pay"},{"key":"B","text":"take"},{"key":"C","text":"bring"},{"key":"D","text":"carry"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"固定搭配pay attention to，意为“注意、关注”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第15题"},{"number":16,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The teacher told the students to ______ their books and turn to page 12.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"open"},{"key":"B","text":"close"},{"key":"C","text":"take"},{"key":"D","text":"lend"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"先打开书，再翻到第12页，选open。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第16题"},{"number":17,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It's no use ______ over spilt milk.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"cry"},{"key":"B","text":"crying"},{"key":"C","text":"to cry"},{"key":"D","text":"cries"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"It's no use doing sth.表示“做某事没有用”。整句意思是覆水难收，后悔无益。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第17题"},{"number":18,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"After the long walk, the children were completely ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tired"},{"key":"B","text":"tiring"},{"key":"C","text":"tire"},{"key":"D","text":"to tire"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"孩子走累了，用tired描述人的感受；tiring表示“令人疲倦的”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第18题"},{"number":19,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He ______ his car keys on the table just now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lay"},{"key":"B","text":"laid"},{"key":"C","text":"lied"},{"key":"D","text":"layed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"此处是“把钥匙放在桌上”：lay的过去式为laid。lie表示“躺”时，过去式才是lay。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第19题"},{"number":20,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"My sister is ______ in music; she can play three instruments.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"interested"},{"key":"B","text":"interesting"},{"key":"C","text":"interest"},{"key":"D","text":"interests"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"be interested in表示“对……感兴趣”；interesting描述事物“有趣”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第20题"},{"number":21,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Could you tell me how ______ the problem?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"solve"},{"key":"B","text":"to solve"},{"key":"C","text":"solving"},{"key":"D","text":"solved"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"疑问词how后接不定式，how to solve意为“如何解决”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第21题"},{"number":22,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He ______ the report when the telephone rang.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reads"},{"key":"B","text":"has read"},{"key":"C","text":"was reading"},{"key":"D","text":"would read"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"电话响时正在读报告：过去进行时表示当时正在进行的动作。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第22题"},{"number":23,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I ______ in this city since I was born.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lived"},{"key":"B","text":"have lived"},{"key":"C","text":"live"},{"key":"D","text":"am living"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"since I was born表示从过去持续到现在，主句用现在完成时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第23题"},{"number":24,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"By the time he arrives, the meeting ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will end"},{"key":"B","text":"will have ended"},{"key":"C","text":"ends"},{"key":"D","text":"has ended"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"by the time he arrives表示“到他到达时”，强调届时已经结束，选将来完成时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第24题"},{"number":25,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"She spends ______ time reading English every day.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"much"},{"key":"B","text":"many"},{"key":"C","text":"a lot"},{"key":"D","text":"few"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"time在这里是不可数名词，用much修饰。a lot若修饰time，须加of。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第25题"},{"number":26,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He asked me ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"where I was going"},{"key":"B","text":"where was I going"},{"key":"C","text":"where I am going"},{"key":"D","text":"where am I going"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"宾语从句用陈述语序；主句asked为过去时，按通常的时态回移选择was going。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第26题"},{"number":27,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"______ we can't understand is ______ he left without saying a word.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What; why"},{"key":"B","text":"That; what"},{"key":"C","text":"What; because"},{"key":"D","text":"Which; how"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"What引导“我们不理解的事情”；why说明不理解的是“他为什么不辞而别”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第27题"},{"number":28,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It was not until she took off her glasses ______ I realized she was my old classmate.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"when"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"then"},{"key":"D","text":"than"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"强调句框架：It was not until...that...，表示“直到……才……”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第28题"},{"number":29,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He speaks English ______ as if he were a native speaker.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so well"},{"key":"B","text":"too well"},{"key":"C","text":"enough well"},{"key":"D","text":"good enough"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"well修饰speaks，so强调程度；整体是“英语说得很好，仿佛是母语者”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第29题"},{"number":30,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"If I ______ harder in high school, I would have a better job now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"study"},{"key":"B","text":"studied"},{"key":"C","text":"had studied"},{"key":"D","text":"would study"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"高中是否努力属于过去，工作好不好是现在：过去条件用had done，现在结果用would do。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第30题"},{"number":31,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Either the teacher or the students ______ to blame for the mistake.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is"},{"key":"B","text":"are"},{"key":"C","text":"was"},{"key":"D","text":"has been"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"either...or...连接主语，谓语通常与靠近它的students保持一致，用复数are。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第31题"},{"number":32,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Hardly ______ down when the phone rang again.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had I sat"},{"key":"B","text":"I had sat"},{"key":"C","text":"did I sit"},{"key":"D","text":"I sat"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"Hardly置于句首，主句部分倒装；Hardly had I done...when...表示“刚……就……”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第32题"},{"number":33,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The book ______ on the table belongs to my brother.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lays"},{"key":"B","text":"lying"},{"key":"C","text":"lies"},{"key":"D","text":"lie"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"句中已有谓语belongs，用lying作后置定语，表示“放在桌上的书”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第33题"},{"number":34,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"______ from the top of the hill, the city looks like a big garden.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Seeing"},{"key":"B","text":"Seen"},{"key":"C","text":"To see"},{"key":"D","text":"See"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"城市是“被看见”的对象，用过去分词Seen。判断分词时先找主句主语the city。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第34题"},{"number":35,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It ______ that the famous singer will come to our city next month.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is said"},{"key":"B","text":"says"},{"key":"C","text":"said"},{"key":"D","text":"is saying"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is said that...表示“据说……”，是常见被动表达。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第35题"},{"number":36,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I don't know ______ he will come or not.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"whether"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"either"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"whether...or not表示“是否”。句子问的是他来不来。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第36题"},{"number":37,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"By next spring, we ______ here for ten years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will live"},{"key":"B","text":"will have lived"},{"key":"C","text":"have lived"},{"key":"D","text":"are living"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"by next spring和for ten years表示到未来某时已持续十年，用将来完成时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第37题"},{"number":38,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I would rather you ______ here tomorrow.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"come"},{"key":"B","text":"came"},{"key":"C","text":"will come"},{"key":"D","text":"coming"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"would rather + 主语 + 过去式，可表达希望别人现在或将来做某事；这里tomorrow指将来。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第38题"},{"number":39,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"My watch is ______; I need to buy a new one.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"break"},{"key":"B","text":"broke"},{"key":"C","text":"broken"},{"key":"D","text":"breaking"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"is broken表示“坏了”。broken作表语描述手表的状态。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第39题"},{"number":40,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"She ______ to the supermarket when I phoned her.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"goes"},{"key":"B","text":"has gone"},{"key":"C","text":"will go"},{"key":"D","text":"was going"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"我打电话时，她正前往超市，用过去进行时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第40题"},{"number":41,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Walking is the best exercise for everyone."},{"key":"B","text":"Walking is simple, useful, and has rules to follow."},{"key":"C","text":"People should walk with friends or family."},{"key":"D","text":"Walking can replace other forms of exercise."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"全文先讲步行方便和益处，再讲步行注意事项；B同时覆盖这两部分。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第41题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":42,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"How long should a person walk each day according to the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Ten minutes."},{"key":"B","text":"Twenty minutes."},{"key":"C","text":"Thirty minutes."},{"key":"D","text":"One hour."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"第1段明确写每天步行三十分钟。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第42题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":43,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"How do you know you are walking at the right speed?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can sing while walking."},{"key":"B","text":"You can talk while walking."},{"key":"C","text":"You cannot talk at all."},{"key":"D","text":"You feel out of breath."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"第2段的完整标准是“不能唱歌，但还能说话”。四个选项中B最接近，不要只记“能说话”而漏掉前半句。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第43题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":44,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Which of the following is NOT mentioned as a rule for walking?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Wear comfortable shoes."},{"key":"B","text":"Drink water before and after walking."},{"key":"C","text":"Walk after a big meal."},{"key":"D","text":"Stop and rest when feeling tired."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"按“哪项不是推荐规则”理解选C。原文明确说不要刚吃完大餐就走；题干用NOT mentioned不够精确，实际是与建议相反。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第44题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":45,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the writer want to tell us in the last sentence?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Walking takes a long time to show results."},{"key":"B","text":"Walking is boring without friends."},{"key":"C","text":"Walking regularly brings both physical and mental benefits."},{"key":"D","text":"Walking is more useful than other sports."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"结尾同时提到body和mind的变化，概括为身体与心理两方面的益处。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第45题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":46,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What should you do first when learning a foreign language?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Listen to English songs."},{"key":"B","text":"Read simple stories."},{"key":"C","text":"Set a clear goal."},{"key":"D","text":"Speak the language."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"第1段明确把设定清晰目标列为第一步。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第46题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":47,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why does the writer say 'Language is sound first'?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Because listening is the most important skill."},{"key":"B","text":"Because we should hear the language before we speak or write."},{"key":"C","text":"Because sounds are easier than words."},{"key":"D","text":"Because music helps learning."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"第2段解释“语言首先是声音”：先多听，再说或写。A把它扩大成“听力最重要”，原文没有这样比较。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第47题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":48,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What should you do when you meet new words while reading?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Look them up at once."},{"key":"B","text":"Stop reading."},{"key":"C","text":"Guess the meaning from the context."},{"key":"D","text":"Write them down at once."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"第3段建议先根据上下文猜词，不要一遇到生词就查词典。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第48题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":49,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the writer say about mistakes?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Mistakes are bad for learning."},{"key":"B","text":"Mistakes show what we still need to learn."},{"key":"C","text":"Only beginners make mistakes."},{"key":"D","text":"We should never make mistakes."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"最后一段认为错误能显示还需要学什么，态度是接受错误、继续尝试。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第49题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":50,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the best title for this passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Why We Learn English."},{"key":"B","text":"Four Steps to Learn a Foreign Language."},{"key":"C","text":"The Importance of Listening."},{"key":"D","text":"Mistakes in Language Learning."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"四步依次是定目标、多听、每天读、不怕犯错；B能覆盖全文。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第50题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":51,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The history of mobile phones."},{"key":"B","text":"The advantages and problems of mobile phones for students."},{"key":"C","text":"How to choose a good phone."},{"key":"D","text":"Why students like phones."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"文章先提手机用途，再重点讨论学生过度使用的问题和合理使用方法；B是现有选项中最全面的。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第51题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":52,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the problem with students who overuse phones?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They spend more time studying."},{"key":"B","text":"They sleep more and feel more energetic."},{"key":"C","text":"They spend less time on homework and feel tired."},{"key":"D","text":"They have higher grades."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"第2段说明玩手机挤占作业等时间，影响成绩并使人疲倦。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第52题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":53,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why does the writer mention 'Holding the phone with the head bent down'?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To show that phones are good."},{"key":"B","text":"To show a healthy way to use phones."},{"key":"C","text":"To show a physical problem caused by phone use."},{"key":"D","text":"To show that phones help us."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"低头用手机导致颈肩不适，是身体方面的问题例子。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第53题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":54,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Which is NOT mentioned as a way to use phones healthily?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Set a time limit each day."},{"key":"B","text":"Keep the phone away during homework."},{"key":"C","text":"Take a short break every hour."},{"key":"D","text":"Use the phone at bedtime."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"末段提出睡前把手机放远；D与建议相反，A、B、C均为文中列出的做法。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第54题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":55,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the writer think of mobile phones?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Phones are bad and should be thrown away."},{"key":"B","text":"Phones are useful when used in the right way."},{"key":"C","text":"Phones are the most important tool."},{"key":"D","text":"Phones are only for adults."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"最后一句强调正确使用时手机才是有用工具；作者并未主张全部丢掉手机。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第55题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":56,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第56空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"good"},{"key":"B","text":"well"},{"key":"C","text":"nice"},{"key":"D","text":"better"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"修饰动词communicate，用副词well。D的better也可表示“沟通得更好”，若含隐含比较也成立；无明确比较时拟选B。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第56题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":57,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第57空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"speak"},{"key":"B","text":"speaking"},{"key":"C","text":"spoken"},{"key":"D","text":"speech"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"与下文listening、speaking呼应，用动名词speaking。D的speech也是名词，放在about后语法并非不成立，但与上下文平行关系较弱。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第57题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":58,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第58空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"speak to"},{"key":"B","text":"talk with"},{"key":"C","text":"treat"},{"key":"D","text":"listen"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"按“我们对待他人的方式”拟选C。但A的speak to和B的talk with都能接others，且句意成立；本题不能认定只有C正确。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第58题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":59,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第59空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"him"},{"key":"B","text":"them"},{"key":"C","text":"her"},{"key":"D","text":"us"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"上文people指复数的人，give后用宾格them。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第59题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":60,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第60空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"good"},{"key":"B","text":"better"},{"key":"C","text":"best"},{"key":"D","text":"well"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"按“认真听便能更好地理解对方”拟选B。D的well也能构成“很好地理解对方”，原文没有强制比较级的形式条件。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第60题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":61,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第61空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"make"},{"key":"B","text":"let"},{"key":"C","text":"ask"},{"key":"D","text":"have"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"make sb. feel comfortable表示“使某人感到舒服”，最符合微笑等带来结果的语义。let、have也能接宾语和动词原形，不能只靠省略to判定A。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第61题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":62,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第62空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"look at"},{"key":"B","text":"look for"},{"key":"C","text":"look up"},{"key":"D","text":"look into"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"交谈时低头“看手机”，会让人觉得你没兴趣，选look at。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第62题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":63,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第63空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"interest"},{"key":"B","text":"interested"},{"key":"C","text":"interesting"},{"key":"D","text":"interests"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"be interested in固定搭配，表示“对谈话感兴趣”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第63题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":64,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第64空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"polite"},{"key":"B","text":"kind"},{"key":"C","text":"difficult"},{"key":"D","text":"rude"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句要求有礼貌、表达清楚，因此不要用粗鲁或太难懂的词。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第64题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":65,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第65空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"step"},{"key":"B","text":"advice"},{"key":"C","text":"way"},{"key":"D","text":"tips"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"these后接可数名词复数，四项只有tips符合；advice不可数，step和way是单数。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第65题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":66,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"The more you practice, the more confident you will become.","options":[],"answer":"你练习得越多，就会变得越自信。","explanation":"the + 比较级..., the + 比较级...：越……，越……。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第66题"},{"number":67,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"It took them three hours to finish the work yesterday.","options":[],"answer":"昨天他们花了三个小时完成这项工作。","explanation":"It took sb. + 时间 + to do：某人花了多少时间做某事；yesterday须译出。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第67题"},{"number":68,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Although he is very young, he can take good care of himself.","options":[],"answer":"虽然他年纪很小，但他能很好地照顾自己。","explanation":"although表示让步；take good care of表示好好照顾；himself指他自己。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第68题"},{"number":69,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"The little girl is too shy to speak in front of the class.","options":[],"answer":"这个小女孩太害羞了，不敢在全班同学面前讲话。","explanation":"too...to...通常表示太……而不能……；这里“不敢讲话”符合shy的语义。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第69题"},{"number":70,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"If I had been there, I would have helped you.","options":[],"answer":"如果我当时在那里，我就会帮你了。","explanation":"had been / would have helped表示与过去事实相反的假设，不要译成一般将来的承诺。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第70题"},{"number":71,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"我花了两小时才完成作业。","options":[],"answer":"It took me two hours to finish my homework.","explanation":"也可译为I spent two hours finishing my homework.；spend后用doing。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第71题"},{"number":72,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"这个故事比那个故事有趣得多。","options":[],"answer":"This story is much more interesting than that one.","explanation":"much修饰比较级，表示“……得多”；interesting的比较级是more interesting。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第72题"},{"number":73,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"我们应该保护眼睛免受电脑屏幕的伤害。","options":[],"answer":"We should protect our eyes from the harm caused by computer screens.","explanation":"protect...from...：保护……免受……；caused by说明伤害的来源。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第73题"},{"number":74,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"如果你努力学习，你的梦想就会实现。","options":[],"answer":"If you study hard, your dream will come true.","explanation":"条件从句用study，主句用will come true；come true表示实现。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第74题"},{"number":75,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"每天早上他都花半小时读英语。","options":[],"answer":"He spends half an hour reading English every morning.","explanation":"每天的习惯用一般现在时；he对应spends；半小时是half an hour。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（一） / 第75题"}],"passages":[{"id":"r1","title":"Walking","paragraphs":["Walking is one of the simplest and most useful forms of exercise. It requires no special equipment, no expensive clothing, and almost everyone can do it. Walking for thirty minutes a day can help people stay healthy in many ways. It strengthens the heart, helps control weight, and improves mood.","Many doctors suggest that people take a brisk walk after dinner. A brisk walk means walking fast enough to raise your breathing, but you should still be able to talk. If you cannot sing but can talk, you are walking at the right speed. Walking with friends or family members makes it more enjoyable. Some people like to listen to music while walking; others prefer to enjoy the scenery.","However, walking also has some rules that you should follow. Wear comfortable shoes. Drink some water before and after walking. If you feel tired or have pain in your chest, stop and rest at once. Don't walk right after a big meal, and avoid walking in very hot or very cold weather. If you keep walking regularly, you will feel the change in your body and mind within a few weeks."],"questionNumbers":[41,42,43,44,45]},{"id":"r2","title":"Learning a Foreign Language","paragraphs":["Learning a foreign language is never easy, but there are some simple ways that can make it easier. The first step is to set a clear goal. Ask yourself why you want to learn the language. Is it for travel, work, or just for fun? A clear goal will keep you going when learning gets hard.","The second step is to listen as much as possible. Language is sound first. Before you speak or write, you need to hear it many times. Watch English movies, listen to English songs, or follow English podcasts. Don't worry about understanding every word at first; just let your ears get used to the sound.","The third step is to read every day. Start with simple stories or news written for learners. Choose books or articles you are interested in. When you meet new words, don't look them up at once. Try to guess the meaning from the context first. Keep a small notebook for new words, but don't write down too many at one time.","Finally, never be afraid of making mistakes. Mistakes show you what you still need to learn. Every successful language learner has made thousands of mistakes. Keep trying, and one day you'll find you can speak the language more easily than you thought."],"questionNumbers":[46,47,48,49,50]},{"id":"r3","title":"Mobile Phones","paragraphs":["Mobile phones have become a big part of our daily life. We use them to make calls, send messages, take photos, pay bills, and even read books. It is hard to imagine a day without a phone. However, the overuse of phones is causing many problems, especially for students.","Many students spend too much time on their phones. They play games for hours, watch short videos, or chat with friends online. As a result, they spend less time on their homework, reading, or even sleeping. Some students check their phones every few minutes, even during class. This hurts their grades and makes them feel tired all day.","Phones also hurt our eyes and bodies. Looking at the screen for a long time can make them dry and sore. Holding the phone with the head bent down hurts the neck and shoulders. Studies show that students who use phones too much often feel more stressed and find it harder to focus.","So how can students use phones in a healthy way? First, set a time limit for phone use each day. Second, keep the phone away when doing homework or at bedtime. Third, take a short break every hour when using the phone. Phones are useful tools, but only when we use them in the right way."],"questionNumbers":[51,52,53,54,55]},{"id":"cloze","title":"有效沟通：听、肢体语言、用词","paragraphs":["Good communication is important in our daily life. When we communicate [56] with others, we can avoid many problems. However, communication is not just about [57]. It is also about listening, body language, and the way we [58] others.","First, listening is as important as speaking. When people are talking to you, please give [59] attention. Don't keep looking at your phone or thinking about other things. If you listen carefully, you will understand the other person [60]. You will also know what to say next.","Second, body language is also part of the way. A smile, a nod, or eye contact can [61] the listener feel comfortable. But if you cross your arms, look away, or [62] your phone, the listener may feel you are not [63] in the talk.","Finally, choose the right words. Don't use words that are too rude or too [64]. Be polite and clear. If you follow these [65], you will become a better communicator and keep better relationships with others."],"questionNumbers":[56,57,58,59,60,61,62,63,64,65]}]},{"id":"mock-2","title":"模拟卷二","subtitle":"团队合作 · 领导沟通 · 诺基亚","description":"根据你提供的参考卷整理，保留原题顺序和选项。","sourceNote":"题目来自继教航标模拟试题（二），答案为逐题核对的参考答案，非出题方公布答案。存疑选择题需对照解析自评。","sourceFiles":"zhen_1.png至zhen_8.png（共8张）","references":[{"title":"[1] Cambridge Grammar / Reason（why、that均可）","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/grammar/british-grammar/reason"},{"title":"[2] British Council / Permission（may not表不允许）","url":"https://learnenglish.britishcouncil.org/free-resources/grammar/english-grammar-reference/permission"},{"title":"[3] Cambridge Grammar / Mind（请求与许可）","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/us/grammar/british-grammar/mind"},{"title":"[4] Cambridge Grammar / British and American English","url":"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/grammar/british-grammar/british-and-american"},{"title":"[5] Oxford Learner's Dictionary / Important（虚拟用法）","url":"https://www.oxfordlearnersdictionaries.com/definition/english/important"}],"minutes":120,"questions":[{"number":1,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- Hi, ______.\n- Nice to meet you. I'm Sarah.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What do you do?"},{"key":"B","text":"I'm 25 years old."},{"key":"C","text":"Let me introduce myself. I'm John."},{"key":"D","text":"May I introduce myself to you?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"对方接着说“很高兴见到你，我是Sarah”，C先介绍自己的姓名，衔接最自然。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第1题"},{"number":2,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- I'm really sorry, I'm late.\n- ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"B","text":"You're welcome."},{"key":"C","text":"Thank you very much."},{"key":"D","text":"That's a good idea."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对迟到道歉回答“没关系”，选A。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第2题"},{"number":3,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- Hello, this is Mr. Smith. May I speak to Tom?\n- ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I don't know you."},{"key":"B","text":"Hold on, please. I'll get him."},{"key":"C","text":"Who are you?"},{"key":"D","text":"Tom has gone home."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"按Tom在场、请其接电话的情景拟选B。如果Tom已经回家，D同样是合理答复；题干未提供排除D的条件。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第3题"},{"number":4,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- Excuse me, could you tell me ______?\n- Sure. It's ten past seven.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"what time is"},{"key":"B","text":"what time it is"},{"key":"C","text":"what is the time"},{"key":"D","text":"what the time"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"could you tell me后接宾语从句，要用陈述语序it is，不能照搬直接问句的is it。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第4题"},{"number":5,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- ______?\n- The black jacket looks great on you.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How do you like my new jacket?"},{"key":"B","text":"Where did you buy the jacket?"},{"key":"C","text":"How much is the jacket?"},{"key":"D","text":"When did you get the jacket?"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"下句说黑夹克穿着好看，回答的是“你觉得我的新夹克怎么样”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第5题"},{"number":6,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- ______?\n- I'd like a coffee and a piece of cake, please.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What do you want to eat?"},{"key":"B","text":"May I take your order?"},{"key":"C","text":"What would you like to have?"},{"key":"D","text":"Both B and C are correct."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"B“可以点餐了吗”和C“想要些什么”都能引出点咖啡、蛋糕。D是说明B和C都对，不是要把这句话放进实际对话。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第6题"},{"number":7,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- Excuse me, could you tell me ______ the nearest subway station?\n- Go straight for two blocks, then turn left.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"where can I get to"},{"key":"B","text":"how can I get to"},{"key":"C","text":"which way is to"},{"key":"D","text":"how I can get to"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"问“如何到最近的地铁站”，宾语从句用I can的陈述语序。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第7题"},{"number":8,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- Would you mind ______ the window?\n- Sure, go ahead.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"open"},{"key":"B","text":"opening"},{"key":"C","text":"to open"},{"key":"D","text":"opened"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"mind后接动名词，语法答案是B。但问句请对方开窗，答句go ahead却许可提问者行动，人物关系不匹配；可将问句改为Would you mind if I opened the window?，或将回答改为Not at all. I will open it.","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第8题"},{"number":9,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- I have a terrible headache. What should I do?\n- ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You'd better go to see a doctor."},{"key":"B","text":"I'm sorry to hear that."},{"key":"C","text":"It doesn't matter."},{"key":"D","text":"That's a good idea."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"对方问What should I do，A直接给出建议。B只表达同情，没有回答应当做什么。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第9题"},{"number":10,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"- It was nice talking to you. ______.\n- Same here. I've got to go too. Have a nice day!","options":[{"key":"A","text":"See you later."},{"key":"B","text":"Take care."},{"key":"C","text":"I've got to go now. Bye."},{"key":"D","text":"Bye-bye."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"下句I've got to go too中的too回应“我也得走了”，与C衔接最紧密。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第10题"},{"number":11,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"If he ______ harder, he will pass the exam.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"studies"},{"key":"B","text":"studied"},{"key":"C","text":"has studied"},{"key":"D","text":"study"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"按将来可能发生的条件理解：主句will pass，if从句用一般现在时；主语he，选studies。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第11题"},{"number":12,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I ______ my keys. I can't find them anywhere.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"lost"},{"key":"B","text":"have lost"},{"key":"C","text":"am losing"},{"key":"D","text":"had lost"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"强调钥匙已丢且现在找不到，用现在完成时最符合本题常规考法。美式英语中A的lost也常用于此语境，不能据此断言A在真实英语中错误。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第12题"},{"number":13,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"While I ______ the dishes, the phone rang.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"wash"},{"key":"B","text":"washed"},{"key":"C","text":"was washing"},{"key":"D","text":"have washed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"电话响时正在洗碗，进行中的背景动作用过去进行时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第13题"},{"number":14,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"By the time you arrive, I ______ dinner.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"finish"},{"key":"B","text":"will finish"},{"key":"C","text":"will have finished"},{"key":"D","text":"have finished"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"by the time you arrive强调“到你来时已经做完”，用将来完成时。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第14题"},{"number":15,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Look! The children ______ in the garden.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"play"},{"key":"B","text":"are playing"},{"key":"C","text":"played"},{"key":"D","text":"have played"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Look!提示眼前正在发生的事情，children是复数，选are playing。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第15题"},{"number":16,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You ______ drive without a license. It's against the law.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"mustn't"},{"key":"B","text":"needn't"},{"key":"C","text":"may not"},{"key":"D","text":"shouldn't"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"后句强调违法，拟选mustn't表示禁止。C的may not也可正式表达“不被允许”，不能把它一概解释成“可能不”。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第16题"},{"number":17,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"She ______ speak three languages when she was only ten.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"can"},{"key":"B","text":"could"},{"key":"C","text":"may"},{"key":"D","text":"might"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"when she was only ten是过去时间，过去的能力用could。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第17题"},{"number":18,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You ______ see the doctor if the cough gets worse.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had better"},{"key":"B","text":"would rather"},{"key":"C","text":"may"},{"key":"D","text":"used to"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"had better do表示“最好做……”，与咳嗽加重时就医的建议相符。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第18题"},{"number":19,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"If I ______ you, I would take the train.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"am"},{"key":"B","text":"was"},{"key":"C","text":"were"},{"key":"D","text":"be"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"If I were you, I would...是给建议的常见虚拟句式，考试中选were。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第19题"},{"number":20,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I wish I ______ harder when I was young.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"studied"},{"key":"B","text":"had studied"},{"key":"C","text":"would study"},{"key":"D","text":"study"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"wish表达对年轻时没更努力的遗憾；与过去事实相反，用过去完成时had studied。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第20题"},{"number":21,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The teacher suggested that each student ______ a summary.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"writes"},{"key":"B","text":"wrote"},{"key":"C","text":"write"},{"key":"D","text":"writing"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"suggest表示建议时，从句可用(should) + 动词原形；主语each student不使此处write变成writes。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第21题"},{"number":22,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It is important that he ______ on time tomorrow.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"arrives"},{"key":"B","text":"arrived"},{"key":"C","text":"arrive"},{"key":"D","text":"will arrive"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"It is important that...在本题考查的虚拟用法中，接(should) arrive。实际用法中也可见普通陈述式arrives，C是按虚拟考法给出的参考选择。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第22题"},{"number":23,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"This novel ______ by a famous Chinese writer in the 1990s.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"wrote"},{"key":"B","text":"was written"},{"key":"C","text":"has written"},{"key":"D","text":"is writing"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"小说是被写出的，in the 1990s为过去时间，选一般过去时的被动结构。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第23题"},{"number":24,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It ______ that the meeting will be held next Monday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is said"},{"key":"B","text":"says"},{"key":"C","text":"has said"},{"key":"D","text":"saying"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"It is said that...表示“据说……”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第24题"},{"number":25,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The building ______ next to the park is a library.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"building"},{"key":"B","text":"built"},{"key":"C","text":"being built"},{"key":"D","text":"to be built"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"暂按已建成理解选B，但题干缺少时间限制。C的being built是正在建，D的to be built是将要建，二者也能成立，本题没有唯一答案。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第25题"},{"number":26,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"______ in 1990, the company now has over 1,000 employees.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Founded"},{"key":"B","text":"Founding"},{"key":"C","text":"Having founded"},{"key":"D","text":"To found"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"公司“被创立于1990年”，用过去分词Founded，与主语the company为被动关系。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第26题"},{"number":27,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Only after he finished his homework ______ to watch TV.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"he was allowed"},{"key":"B","text":"was he allowed"},{"key":"C","text":"he allowed"},{"key":"D","text":"did he allow"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Only + 状语置句首，主句部分倒装；he与allow为被动关系，因此是was he allowed。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第27题"},{"number":28,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Not until he took off his glasses ______ who he was.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I did realize"},{"key":"B","text":"did I realize"},{"key":"C","text":"I realized"},{"key":"D","text":"had I realized"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Not until...置句首，主句倒装；过去的一次“意识到”用did + 主语 + realize。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第28题"},{"number":29,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It was in Beijing ______ I first met my best friend.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"which"},{"key":"C","text":"where"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"强调地点的结构：It was in Beijing that...。去掉It was和that，原句仍完整。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第29题"},{"number":30,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"______ you started early, you would have caught the train.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"If"},{"key":"B","text":"Had"},{"key":"C","text":"Should"},{"key":"D","text":"Were"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"Had you started early相当于If you had started early，是过去虚拟条件省略if后的倒装。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第30题"},{"number":31,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The book ______ I bought yesterday is very interesting.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"who"},{"key":"B","text":"whom"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"先行词book为物，关系词在从句中作bought的宾语，选which。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第31题"},{"number":32,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"This is the house ______ I lived three years ago.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"where"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"从句I lived中不缺宾语，缺“住在哪里”的地点状语，所以用where。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第32题"},{"number":33,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I don't know ______ he will come or not.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"whether"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"which"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"whether...or not表示“是否”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第33题"},{"number":34,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The reason ______ he was late is that he missed the bus.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"why"},{"key":"D","text":"for that"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"按常见框架The reason why...is that...拟选C。但The reason that he was late...也成立，B不能排除。","reviewRequired":true,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第34题"},{"number":35,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He took a taxi so that he ______ get there on time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"can"},{"key":"B","text":"may"},{"key":"C","text":"could"},{"key":"D","text":"must"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"主句took为过去时，目的从句用could get there，表示为了能及时到达。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第35题"},{"number":36,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"She is ______ of dogs. She has three at home.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"afraid"},{"key":"B","text":"tired"},{"key":"C","text":"fond"},{"key":"D","text":"proud"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"be fond of表示“喜欢”；养三只狗支持“喜欢狗”的理解。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第36题"},{"number":37,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"______ your help, I passed the exam.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"With"},{"key":"B","text":"For"},{"key":"C","text":"By"},{"key":"D","text":"Because"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"With your help意为“在你的帮助下”。Because后不能直接接your help，需because of。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第37题"},{"number":38,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"He is ______ late for class. He always arrives on time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"often"},{"key":"B","text":"always"},{"key":"C","text":"seldom"},{"key":"D","text":"ever"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后句说他总是准时，只有seldom“很少”最接近“不迟到”的方向；严格说与always仍有轻微程度差别。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第38题"},{"number":39,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The two friends haven't seen each other ______ five years.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"since"},{"key":"B","text":"for"},{"key":"C","text":"during"},{"key":"D","text":"from"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"for接持续的时长five years；since通常接时间起点。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第39题"},{"number":40,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"I have nothing ______ to say on this matter.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"farther"},{"key":"B","text":"far"},{"key":"C","text":"more"},{"key":"D","text":"less"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"nothing more to say表示“没有更多要说的了”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第40题"},{"number":41,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the main idea of the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Team building events are usually fun activities in a cafeteria."},{"key":"B","text":"Team members should focus on their own work rather than helping others."},{"key":"C","text":"Sharing and cooperation make a team more effective than working alone."},{"key":"D","text":"Balloon games are a good way to test team members' personal skills."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"只找自己的气球，15分钟没人找到；互相交还气球，2分钟全部完成。对比说明合作更有效。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第41题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":42,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why did the team leader bring the 35 employees into the cafeteria?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To celebrate the end of a project."},{"key":"B","text":"Because the team members wouldn't share information with each other."},{"key":"C","text":"To introduce a new employee to the others."},{"key":"D","text":"Because the leader was bored with normal meetings."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"第1段交代问题是成员不愿分享信息或解决办法，活动正是为解决这一问题。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第42题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":43,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"How many team members successfully wrote their names on the balloons at first?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"About 15."},{"key":"B","text":"About 30."},{"key":"C","text":"About 35."},{"key":"D","text":"About 5."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"第2段写约30人成功写上姓名而没有弄破气球。35是参加活动的总人数，不能混用。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第43题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":44,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the purpose of the third round of the activity?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To reward the fastest team members."},{"key":"B","text":"To let members practice blowing up balloons."},{"key":"C","text":"To teach members to help each other find their balloons."},{"key":"D","text":"To pick a leader for the next activity."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"第3轮让大家拿到有名字的气球就交给对应的人，用实际行动体验互助。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第44题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":45,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"The word 'obstacles' in the last paragraph is closest in meaning to ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"rules"},{"key":"B","text":"barriers"},{"key":"C","text":"games"},{"key":"D","text":"leaders"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"末段说只顾个人目标会给团队制造obstacles，即“障碍”，与barriers同义。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第45题","passageId":"r1"},{"number":46,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"How to become an excellent public speaker."},{"key":"B","text":"Five communication habits that effective leaders share."},{"key":"C","text":"Why trust is the most important thing in business."},{"key":"D","text":"The history of leadership communication styles."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"开头明确介绍有效领导者的五项沟通做法，后文逐项展开。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第46题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":47,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"According to the passage, what should leaders avoid in their communication?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Speaking too quietly."},{"key":"B","text":"Asking questions too often."},{"key":"C","text":"Using technical jargon and business speak."},{"key":"D","text":"Sending emails to employees."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"有关简化表达的一段要求避免增加理解负担的技术术语和商业套话。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第47题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":48,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why does the author mention 'visibility' in the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To suggest leaders should post more about their daily life online."},{"key":"B","text":"To show that leaders should appear in person and build real connections."},{"key":"C","text":"To warn that being seen too often may cause problems."},{"key":"D","text":"To explain how to design a company website."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"visibility一段强调面对面交流，不能只躲在电脑后面，通过真实互动建立联系。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第48题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":49,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the author mean by 'read between the lines'?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Read every word in the message carefully."},{"key":"B","text":"Ignore what people say and only watch their actions."},{"key":"C","text":"Understand what people really mean beyond their words."},{"key":"D","text":"Write longer emails with more details."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"因下属未必直接表达意见，要结合非语言线索理解言外之意；不是忽略说话内容。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第49题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":50,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"The word 'eloquence' in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"friendliness"},{"key":"B","text":"fluency / skill in speaking"},{"key":"C","text":"silence"},{"key":"D","text":"honesty"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"eloquence表示雄辩或善于表达。该段主张真实清楚，不要只追求辞藻与口才。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第50题","passageId":"r2"},{"number":51,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"According to the passage, what is the main reason for Nokia's failure in the smartphone market?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Their products were technically worse than Apple's."},{"key":"B","text":"They were too comfortable and slow to act."},{"key":"C","text":"A culture of fear inside the company froze decision-making."},{"key":"D","text":"Their platform environment was poor."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"全文核心解释是恐惧造成公司行动停滞。第一段所列技术、安于现状、平台问题是随后被质疑的解释。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第51题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":52,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"How did the researchers reach their conclusion?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By reading news articles about Nokia."},{"key":"B","text":"By interviewing top and middle managers, engineers and outside experts."},{"key":"C","text":"By comparing Nokia's products with Apple's."},{"key":"D","text":"By asking customers about their phones."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"研究依据包含深入调查和76次访谈，访谈对象正是高层、中层、工程师及外部专家。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第52题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":53,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why did middle managers lie to top managers?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They wanted to get more money from the company."},{"key":"B","text":"They were afraid of being shouted at and losing resources."},{"key":"C","text":"They didn't like Apple's products."},{"key":"D","text":"They thought top managers would agree with them."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"文章既说高层常大声训斥，也说中层担心报告坏消息后失去资源，所以报喜不报忧。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第53题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":54,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the author mean by describing top managers as 'extremely temperamental'?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They were calm and patient with their staff."},{"key":"B","text":"They were friendly and easy to talk to."},{"key":"C","text":"They had sudden changes in mood and could be angry easily."},{"key":"D","text":"They were slow in making decisions."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"后文用大声喊叫说明temperamental，语境指脾气多变、容易发怒。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第54题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":55,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What lesson does the passage offer to today's leaders?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"A little fear is good, but too much fear can be harmful to a company."},{"key":"B","text":"Leaders should shout at their staff to keep them alert."},{"key":"C","text":"Companies should ignore middle managers' opinions."},{"key":"D","text":"Fear is always a useful tool for motivation."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"结尾区分适度恐惧和滥用恐惧，强调后者有副作用，并非认为恐惧始终有用。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第55题","passageId":"r3"},{"number":56,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第56空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"give up"},{"key":"B","text":"give away"},{"key":"C","text":"give in"},{"key":"D","text":"put up"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"这里是“牺牲、让出自己的空闲时间帮助别人”。give in是让步，put up不合句意。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第56题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":57,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第57空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"each"},{"key":"B","text":"other"},{"key":"C","text":"others"},{"key":"D","text":"another"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"some...some...others...表示“一些人……一些人……还有一些人……”。others独立指其他人。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第57题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":58,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第58空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"such"},{"key":"B","text":"many"},{"key":"C","text":"much"},{"key":"D","text":"a"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"one of many volunteers表示“许多志愿者中的一位”；much不能修饰可数复数volunteers。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第58题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":59,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第59空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"for"},{"key":"B","text":"since"},{"key":"C","text":"from"},{"key":"D","text":"when"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"主句has been helping表示一直在帮助，since接起点“她十六岁时”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第59题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":60,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第60空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"early"},{"key":"B","text":"earlier"},{"key":"C","text":"earliest"},{"key":"D","text":"more early"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"than anyone else提示比较，early的比较级是earlier。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第60题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":61,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第61空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bright"},{"key":"B","text":"brightly"},{"key":"C","text":"brightness"},{"key":"D","text":"brightened"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"make + 宾语 + 形容词：孩子们的笑容让她一整天都明亮、愉快。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第61题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":62,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第62空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"said"},{"key":"B","text":"asked"},{"key":"C","text":"made"},{"key":"D","text":"let"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"ask sb. to do sth.表示请某人做某事。make和let通常接不带to的不定式，本题to已给出。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第62题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":63,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第63空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"borrowed"},{"key":"B","text":"lent"},{"key":"C","text":"collected"},{"key":"D","text":"offered"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"book drive是图书募集活动，因此三个月内是“募集到”1000多本书，选collected。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第63题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":64,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第64空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"whatever"},{"key":"B","text":"wherever"},{"key":"C","text":"no matter what"},{"key":"D","text":"however"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"however + 形容词 + 主语 + 谓语，表示“不管……多么……”。本句即“不管努力看起来多么微小”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第64题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":65,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第65空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tells"},{"key":"B","text":"speaks"},{"key":"C","text":"says"},{"key":"D","text":"talks"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"tell sb.可以直接接us；say通常说say to us，speak或talk则通常搭配to/with。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第65题","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":66,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Most of us have to learn to manage ourselves, because companies no longer manage their employees' entire careers the way they once did.","options":[],"answer":"我们大多数人都必须学会自我管理，因为公司不再像过去那样管理员工的整个职业生涯。","explanation":"no longer：不再；the way they once did：像过去那样。did代替前文的管理行为。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第66题"},{"number":67,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"The instructor asked us to break into small groups, and then each group discussed how to cooperate better in the team.","options":[],"answer":"指导老师让我们分成小组，然后各组讨论了如何在团队中更好地合作。","explanation":"break into small groups：分成小组，不是“闯入”；how to cooperate：如何合作。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第67题"},{"number":68,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"She is a very influential leader because she always expresses her ideas in simple and clear language.","options":[],"answer":"她是一位很有影响力的领导者，因为她总是用简单清晰的语言表达自己的想法。","explanation":"influential：有影响力的；in...language表示用某种语言或表达方式。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第68题"},{"number":69,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Research shows that staying in a fear-filled environment for a long time will make employees afraid to speak their true thoughts.","options":[],"answer":"研究表明，长期处于充满恐惧的环境中，会使员工不敢说出自己的真实想法。","explanation":"staying...作从句的主语；make employees afraid：使员工害怕。译文须保留“长期”和“真实”。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第69题"},{"number":70,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Although he is rich, he still walks to work every day to keep fit.","options":[],"answer":"虽然他很富有，但他仍然每天步行上班，以保持健康。","explanation":"walk to work：步行上班；to keep fit表目的；still是仍然。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第70题"},{"number":71,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"许多公司发现，好的团队建设活动可以极大地提高员工的合作能力。","options":[],"answer":"Many companies have found that good team-building activities can greatly improve employees' ability to cooperate.","explanation":"greatly表示极大地；ability to cooperate表示合作能力；found/have found的选择可随上下文调整。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第71题"},{"number":72,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"有效的沟通不仅需要良好的表达能力，还需要认真倾听的能力。","options":[],"answer":"Effective communication requires not only good speaking skills but also the ability to listen carefully.","explanation":"not only...but also...：不仅……而且……；speaking skills与the ability to listen并列作宾语。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第72题"},{"number":73,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"如果想让你的团队取得成功，你必须学会信任每一位成员，并重视他们的想法。","options":[],"answer":"If you want your team to succeed, you must learn to trust every member and value their ideas.","explanation":"want sb. to do：想让某人做；value作动词，表示重视；every member表示每一位成员。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第73题"},{"number":74,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"健康的企业文化鼓励员工大胆分享自己的观点，而不用担心受到惩罚。","options":[],"answer":"A healthy corporate culture encourages employees to share their views openly without fear of punishment.","explanation":"encourage sb. to do：鼓励某人做；openly体现大胆、公开地；without fear of punishment表示不担心受罚。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第74题"},{"number":75,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"经理决定每周一上午开一个简短的会议，这样每个人都能及时了解最新的进展情况。","options":[],"answer":"The manager decided to hold a brief meeting every Monday morning so that everyone could stay up to date with the latest developments.","explanation":"decide to do：决定做；so that表示目的；stay up to date with表示及时了解最新情况。","reviewRequired":false,"source":"继教航标模拟试题（二） / 第75题"}],"passages":[{"id":"r1","title":"A Teamwork Game","paragraphs":["A team of about 35 employees had come together for a team building event. They were a young, bright and enthusiastic team. However, one of their chief problems was the fact that they wouldn't share information or solutions with each other, and the team leader thought they were too focused on themselves and not on the team. As a result, she brought them all into the cafeteria. All of the tables and chairs had been stored away, and fun decorations and hundreds of different colored balloons had been placed around the room.","In the center of the room was a big box of balloons that hadn't been blown up yet. The team leader instructed everybody to pick a balloon, blow it up, and write their name on it, but they had to be careful not to burst the balloon. Although they were given a second chance if their first balloon popped, they were out of the game the second time round. In the end, about 30 team members wrote their names without their balloons popping. They were then asked to leave the room and, after five minutes, the team leader brought them back in and asked them to find the balloon with their name on it amongst the hundreds of other balloons in the room. After 15 minutes of searching, no one had found their balloon, and the team were told that they were then going to move on to the third round of the activity.","In this round, each team member was instructed to find any balloon with a name on it and then give that balloon to the person whose name was on it. Within two minutes, everybody had their own balloon. The team leader summarized the activity thus: “We are much more efficient when we are willing to share with each other and much better at problem solving when we are working together, not individually.”","Sometimes, members of teams create obstacles by focusing solely on their own pursuits and goals. Every member of the team should ask themselves on a regular basis what they are doing and what they can do for the team."],"questionNumbers":[41,42,43,44,45]},{"id":"r2","title":"Habits of Highly Effective Communicators","paragraphs":["It's no secret that good leaders are also good communicators. Indeed, communication and leadership are inextricably tied. How can you inspire or guide others if you don't communicate in a clear, credible and authentic way? Here are five essential communication practices of effective leaders:","Trust is the bedrock of effective leadership - your behavior is your single greatest mode of communication, and it must be congruent with what you say. If your actions don't align with your words, trust quickly breaks down.","Effective leaders distill complex thoughts and strategies into simple, memorable terms that colleagues and customers can grasp and act upon. The most important thing is to clarify what you want to say, look out for technical jargon and avoid business speak, which add complexity. Say what you mean in as few words as possible.","Use language that's distinctly your own; let your values come through in your communication. Correct use of language and grammar is important, of course, but don't become overly fixated on eloquence for eloquence's sake; concentrate on being distinct and real. People want real, and people respect real.","Visibility is about letting your key stakeholders get a feel for who you are and what you care about. Don't hide behind a computer and only interact with people electronically - see them face to face and voice to voice, and interact with them in a real, substantial way. In today's environment, where people are often burned out, it's important for employees to have a personal connection with you and the work you believe in. Show the people who work for you that you're engaged and you care about them and their work.","Effective communication is a two-way process, and good leaders know how to ask good questions, and then listen with both their eyes and their ears. Because you are in a position of authority, others may be reluctant to express their real opinions to you directly. You won't always get direct feedback, so you also need to be able to read between the lines and look for the non-verbal cues."],"questionNumbers":[46,47,48,49,50]},{"id":"r3","title":"Who Killed Nokia?","paragraphs":["Nokia executives attempted to explain its fall from the top of the smartphone pyramid with three factors: first, that Nokia was technically inferior to Apple; second, that the company was complacent; and third, that its platform environment was poor.","It has also been argued that it was none of the above. Nokia lost the smartphone battle because of divergent shared fears among the company's middle and top managers, which led to company-wide inertia.","Based on the findings of an in-depth investigation and 76 interviews with top and middle managers, engineers and external experts, the researchers discovered a culture of fear due to temperamental leaders and that frightened middle managers were scared of telling the truth.","The fear that froze the company came from two places. First, the company's top managers had a terrifying reputation. Some members of Nokia's board and top management were described as \"extremely temperamental\" and they regularly shouted at people \"at the top of their lungs\". It was very difficult to tell them things they didn't want to hear. Second, top managers were afraid of the external environment and not meeting their quarterly targets, which also impacted how they treated middle managers.","Top managers thus made middle managers afraid of disappointing them. Middle managers were told that they were not ambitious enough to meet top managers' goals.","Fearing the reactions of top managers, middle managers remained silent or provided optimistic, filtered information. Thus, middle managers directly lied to top management.","What was worse, a culture of status inside Nokia made everyone want to hold onto vested power for fear of resources being allocated elsewhere if they delivered bad news or showed that they were not bold or ambitious enough.","Beyond verbal pressure, top managers also applied pressure for faster performance in personnel selection. This led middle managers to over promise and under deliver. One middle manager told us that \"you can get resources by promising something earlier, or promising a lot. It's sales work\".","While modest fear might be healthy for motivation, abusing it can be like overusing a drug, which risks generating harmful side effects. To reduce this risk, leaders should coordinate with the varied emotions of the staff."],"questionNumbers":[51,52,53,54,55]},{"id":"cloze","title":"志愿服务与图书募集","paragraphs":["Volunteers play an important role in our communities. Every weekend, hundreds of people [56] their free time to help others. Some visit old people's homes, some clean up city parks, and [57] teach children to read. Jane is one of [58] volunteers. She has been helping at a local reading center [59] she was sixteen. Every Saturday morning, she arrives at the center [60] than anyone else. \"I love being here,\" she says. \"The smiles on the children's faces make my whole day [61].\" Last year, Jane [62] her friends to start a book drive. Within three months, they [63] over 1,000 books for children in need. Jane believes that everyone can make a difference, [64] small the effort may seem. \"You don't have to be rich or famous to help others,\" Jane [65] us. \"Sometimes, all it takes is a little time and a warm heart.\""],"questionNumbers":[56,57,58,59,60,61,62,63,64,65]}]},{"id":"comprehensive-2026","title":"考前综合练习卷","subtitle":"亲子沟通 · 团队合作 · 汽车防盗","description":"刚整理的完整练习卷，附小白解析与记法。","sourceNote":"50道交际、词汇语法和翻译题选自30天原资料；阅读和完形25题依据本地教材文章编制。本卷为综合练习，不是已经确认的今年考试原卷。","minutes":120,"questions":[{"number":1,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Hello, may I speak to Mike? _____. May I ask who is calling?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm Mike."},{"key":"B","text":"This is Mike myself."},{"key":"C","text":"This is Mike speaking."},{"key":"D","text":"You are speaking to myself."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：对方打电话找Mike，接电话的人确认自己就是Mike。\n判断：电话里自报身份常用 This is ... speaking。后面的 who is calling 也说明这是电话场景。\n排除：This is Mike myself 搭配不自然；You are speaking to myself 把反身代词用错了。\n记法：电话自报家门：This is ... speaking。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md 第24题"},{"number":2,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Thank you for all your hard work! _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"You can say that."},{"key":"B","text":"Why do you say so?"},{"key":"C","text":"No, thanks."},{"key":"D","text":"You're welcome!"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：对方感谢你付出的辛勤劳动。\n判断：别人说 Thank you，回答 You are welcome，意思是“不客气”。\n排除：No, thanks 是婉拒别人的好意，不是回应感谢。\n记法：谢谢你 → 不客气。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md 第14题"},{"number":3,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"What a beautiful hat you are wearing today! _____. It's nice of you to say so.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Not at all."},{"key":"B","text":"Never mind."},{"key":"C","text":"Oh, no."},{"key":"D","text":"Thanks"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：对方夸你今天的帽子漂亮。\n判断：赞美之后先说 Thanks；后面的“你这样说真好”继续表达感谢。\n排除：Never mind 常表示“别介意”；Oh, no 直接否认，不如感谢自然。\n记法：听到夸奖，先道谢。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md 第11题"},{"number":4,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I was worried about my maths, but Mr. Brown gave me an A. _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Don't worry about it."},{"key":"B","text":"Congratulations!"},{"key":"C","text":"Mr. Brown is very good."},{"key":"D","text":"Good luck to you."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：对方原本担心数学成绩，结果拿到了A。\n判断：好成绩已经取得，用 Congratulations 表示祝贺。\n排除：Good luck 用在事情发生前，祝愿对方好运。\n记法：事前祝好运，事后说祝贺。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md 第13题"},{"number":5,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"I'm leaving for Shanghai tomorrow. _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"See you later."},{"key":"B","text":"Have a pleasant trip!"},{"key":"C","text":"Let's go out for a drink."},{"key":"D","text":"Nice meeting you."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：对方说明天要去上海。\n判断：Have a pleasant trip 是针对旅行的祝愿，最切合对方提到的行程。\n排除：See you later 只是告别，没有像B那样回应旅行这条信息。\n记法：说到出行，想到 trip。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md 第9题"},{"number":6,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"How about going to dinner at the Italian restaurant tonight? _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Sorry."},{"key":"B","text":"That's great."},{"key":"C","text":"Forget it."},{"key":"D","text":"Glad you like it."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：对方建议今晚去意大利餐馆吃饭。\n判断：How about ...? 在提建议，That’s great 表示接受并觉得不错。\n排除：Glad you like it 回应别人喜欢某物；Forget it 是“算了”。\n记法：How about 提建议；That’s great 表接受。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md 第14题"},{"number":7,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Would you mind my turning on the heating system? The temperature goes too low. _____. I feel a little bit cold as well.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Yes, I'd love to."},{"key":"B","text":"Of course."},{"key":"C","text":"No, I don't care."},{"key":"D","text":"Of course not."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：对方问是否介意他打开暖气，你也觉得冷。\n判断：Would you mind ...? 问的是“介意吗”。Of course not 表示不介意，和后句“我也冷”一致。\n排除：Of course 单独回答容易表示“当然介意”；不能把 mind 问句简单当成想不想的问句。\n记法：mind 问介意；同意对方做，就说不介意。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第20题"},{"number":8,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Henry, I think Team Tiger will win the game. _____. I think Team Bull will.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I don't think so."},{"key":"B","text":"I hope so."},{"key":"C","text":"Neither do"},{"key":"D","text":"Me too."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：一人看好Tiger队，另一人看好Bull队。\n判断：后一句支持另一支队伍，所以前面应表示不赞同：I don’t think so。\n排除：Me too 表示“我也是”，与后面的不同预测矛盾。\n记法：先看后半句，再判同不同意。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md 第2题"},{"number":9,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"Sorry to interrupt your phone call. This is a library, and you are talking too loudly. _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I'm sorry."},{"key":"B","text":"Am I talking quietly?"},{"key":"C","text":"That's OK."},{"key":"D","text":"You are welcome."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：你在图书馆打电话太大声，被人提醒。\n判断：造成了打扰，应说 I’m sorry。对方开头的 Sorry 只是礼貌打断，并不是题目让你接受道歉。\n排除：You are welcome 用来回应感谢；That’s OK 不能恰当地为自己的大声说话道歉。\n记法：看清谁做错事，别只盯第一个 Sorry。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md 第30题"},{"number":10,"section":0,"points":1,"stem":"_____? The one who is slim and wears a blue dress.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"What's the lady?"},{"key":"B","text":"What's your English teacher like?"},{"key":"C","text":"Which girl do you want to see?"},{"key":"D","text":"What does your girlfriend look like?"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：回答者指出那个身材苗条、穿蓝裙子的女孩。\n判断：The one ... 在从人群中辨认某一个，因此应问 Which girl。\n排除：只问外貌不能像 Which girl 一样直接对应 The one 的指认。\n记法：The one 在指人，前面常问哪一个。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md 第2题"},{"number":11,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Her determination to _____ her goal of life motivated her greater effort.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"retain"},{"key":"B","text":"attain"},{"key":"C","text":"contain"},{"key":"D","text":"entertain"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：她实现人生目标的决心激励她更加努力。\n判断：attain a goal 是“实现目标”。\n排除：retain 保留，contain 包含，entertain 招待或使愉快，都不能表达实现目标。\n记法：目标要实现：attain a goal。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md 第21题"},{"number":12,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"About two thirds of the students _____ the meeting yesterday.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"attended"},{"key":"B","text":"attend"},{"key":"C","text":"attends"},{"key":"D","text":"was attending"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：昨天大约三分之二的学生参加了会议。\n判断：yesterday 给出过去时间，句子陈述已经发生的事，用 attended。\n排除：attend、attends 是一般现在时；was attending 与复数主语 students 不一致。\n记法：先找时间词：yesterday 提示过去。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第21题"},{"number":13,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The government is spending more and more money to make better medical service _____ to the farmers.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reasonable"},{"key":"B","text":"accessible"},{"key":"C","text":"acceptable"},{"key":"D","text":"sensible"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：政府投入更多资金，让农民能获得更好的医疗服务。\n判断：accessible to somebody 表示某人能够接近、使用或获得。这里说的是医疗服务的可获得性。\n排除：reasonable 合理的，acceptable 可接受的，sensible 明智的；不要把“能获得”当成“能接受”。\n记法：能接触、能使用：accessible。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md 第28题"},{"number":14,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"We _____ for 13 hours by the time we get to New York.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"will fly"},{"key":"B","text":"will have flown"},{"key":"C","text":"flew"},{"key":"D","text":"fly"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：到达纽约时，我们将已经飞行了十三个小时。\n判断：by the time 引导未来时间点，主句描述到那时已完成的飞行时长，用 will have flown。\n排除：will fly 只表示将来，不如将来完成时突出“到那时已经”；flew 是过去。\n记法：到将来某时已经完成：will have done。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md 第12题"},{"number":15,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The company drew up a thorough plan about the advertising campaign in order to _____ sales.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"achieve"},{"key":"B","text":"boost"},{"key":"C","text":"produce"},{"key":"D","text":"yield"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：公司制订广告计划，目的是促进销售。\n判断：boost sales 是提高、促进销量。\n排除：achieve 常与目标搭配；produce 生产；yield 产出。此处重点是提高销量。\n记法：促进销量：boost sales。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md 第12题"},{"number":16,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The classroom _____ since last Friday, so it is clean and tidy now.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had been cleaned"},{"key":"B","text":"was cleaned"},{"key":"C","text":"is cleaned"},{"key":"D","text":"has been cleaned"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：从上周五到现在，教室已经得到清扫，现在很整洁。\n判断：since last Friday 把过去与现在连接起来，且教室是被清扫的，所以用 has been cleaned。\n排除：had been cleaned 需要过去的参照点；这里的 now 指向现在。一般现在时也没有体现这段时间。\n记法：过去延续到现在：has/have；被做过：has/have been done。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二十二天.md 第12题"},{"number":17,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"We are professional movers and we have _____ special protective measures.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"addressed"},{"key":"B","text":"addicted"},{"key":"C","text":"adapted"},{"key":"D","text":"adopted"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：专业搬家公司采取了特别的保护措施。\n判断：adopt measures 表示采取措施。\n排除：adapt 是适应或改编；addicted 是上瘾的；addressed 不是“采取措施”的搭配。\n记法：adopt 采用；adapt 适应。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十八天.md 第16题"},{"number":18,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Sally as well as her brother _____ reading books.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"likes"},{"key":"B","text":"like"},{"key":"C","text":"have liked"},{"key":"D","text":"is liking"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：莎莉和她的哥哥都喜欢读书。\n判断：主语中心是 Sally，as well as her brother 是附加部分，一般现在时用 likes。\n排除：have liked 与单数主语不合；本句表达一般喜好，通常不用 is liking。\n记法：as well as 不把单数主语变复数。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md 第6题"},{"number":19,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Tom _____ more than twenty pounds for the dictionary.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"spent"},{"key":"B","text":"paid"},{"key":"C","text":"cost"},{"key":"D","text":"took"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：汤姆为那本词典付了二十多英镑。\n判断：主语是人，后面已有 for，选择 paid：人 + pay + 钱 + for + 物。\n排除：spend 通常搭配 on 或 doing；cost 的主语通常是物；take 常用于花费时间的结构。\n记法：人付款 pay for；人花费 spend on。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md 第22题"},{"number":20,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"This is the book _____ I have learned a lot.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to which"},{"key":"B","text":"that"},{"key":"C","text":"from which"},{"key":"D","text":"of which"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：这就是让我学到很多东西的那本书。\n判断：先还原 learn a lot from the book，再把 the book 换成 which，得到 from which。\n排除：不能只因先行词是 book 就选 that；这里 learn 后的来源关系需要 from。\n记法：先还原搭配，再选介词：learn from。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第九天.md 第28题"},{"number":21,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The governor had to _____ all his appointments for the day and rush to the train accident.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"set off"},{"key":"B","text":"pay off"},{"key":"C","text":"see off"},{"key":"D","text":"call off"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：州长取消当天全部约见，赶去火车事故现场。\n判断：call off 表示取消，符合临时中断当天安排的语境。\n排除：set off 出发；pay off 还清或取得回报；see off 送行。\n记法：取消活动：call off。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md 第16题"},{"number":22,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"How long do you think _____ to finish this urgent task?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"did it take you"},{"key":"B","text":"it will take you"},{"key":"C","text":"will it take you"},{"key":"D","text":"it to take you"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：你认为完成这项紧急任务需要多长时间？\n判断：核心结构是 it takes ... to do；do you think 后保持 it will take 的陈述语序。\n排除：不要在 do you think 后再次把 will 放到 it 前面，也不能把主语或谓语漏掉。\n记法：疑问句外面已倒装，里面保持主语在前。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第一天.md 第1题"},{"number":23,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The boy's laziness _____ his failure in the exams.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"occurred to"},{"key":"B","text":"brought in"},{"key":"C","text":"resulted in"},{"key":"D","text":"led into"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：这个男孩因为懒惰而考试失败。\n判断：懒惰是原因，失败是结果，因此用 resulted in。\n排除：occur to 表示想到；bring in 引入；表示导致通常说 lead to，而题中给的是 led into。\n记法：原因 result in 结果；结果 result from 原因。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二天.md 第3题"},{"number":24,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You don't mind _____ you Jenny, do you?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"I called"},{"key":"B","text":"to call"},{"key":"C","text":"to be called"},{"key":"D","text":"my calling"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：你不介意我叫你Jenny，对吗？\n判断：mind 后接 doing。my calling 表示“我这样称呼你”这件事。\n排除：不能说 mind to call；I called 是独立主谓结构，不能直接放在这里。\n记法：介意做某事：mind doing。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十七天.md 第10题"},{"number":25,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You should be content _____ what you have.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to"},{"key":"B","text":"about"},{"key":"C","text":"with"},{"key":"D","text":"for"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：你应当满足于自己拥有的东西。\n判断：be content with 是“对……感到满足”的固定搭配。\n排除：这里的 content 是形容词，不是“内容”这个名词；后面的介词用 with。\n记法：对已有的满足：be content with。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md 第3题"},{"number":26,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The first book _____ for English teaching came out in the 16th century.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"written"},{"key":"B","text":"writing"},{"key":"C","text":"to write"},{"key":"D","text":"wrote"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：第一本用于英语教学的书在十六世纪出版。\n判断：书是被写的，written 修饰 book，相当于 which was written。\n排除：writing 表示主动；wrote 是过去式谓语，不能直接这样修饰 book。\n记法：名词被做某事，用过去分词修饰。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十四天.md 第30题"},{"number":27,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The customer service representatives often allow customers to exchange the item or return it for a full _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"reform"},{"key":"B","text":"refund"},{"key":"C","text":"refusal"},{"key":"D","text":"refreshment"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：客服通常允许顾客换货，或者退货并获得全额退款。\n判断：退货后拿回的钱是 refund，full refund 即全额退款。\n排除：refusal 拒绝，reform 改革，refreshment 点心或恢复精神，都不是退款。\n记法：退回的钱：refund。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md 第24题"},{"number":28,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"They got there an hour _____ than others.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"early"},{"key":"B","text":"much early"},{"key":"C","text":"more early"},{"key":"D","text":"earlier"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：他们比其他人早到一小时。\n判断：than 提示比较；early 的比较级是 earlier。\n排除：不能写 more early；much early 也不是这里需要的比较级形式。\n记法：有 than，检查比较级。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第12题"},{"number":29,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Children tend to copy the behaviour of others whom they admire or _____ with.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"identify"},{"key":"B","text":"recognize"},{"key":"C","text":"emphasize"},{"key":"D","text":"justify"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：孩子倾向于模仿他们崇拜或认同的人的行为。\n判断：identify with somebody 表示认同某人，和前面的 admire 构成并列。\n排除：recognize 是认出；emphasize 强调；justify 证明合理，均不构成本题所需的搭配。\n记法：认同某人：identify with。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md 第27题"},{"number":30,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"It was not until nearly a month later _____ I received the manager's reply.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"which"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"that"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：直到将近一个月后，我才收到经理的回复。\n判断：强调结构为 It was not until ... that ...。\n排除：when 虽与时间有关，但这里应先识别 It was ... that 的强调框架。\n记法：强调“直到才”：It was not until ... that ...。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十三天.md 第5题"},{"number":31,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Unfortunately, _____ bad weather, this year's show has been canceled.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"due to"},{"key":"B","text":"despite"},{"key":"C","text":"because"},{"key":"D","text":"since"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：由于天气不好，今年的演出取消了。\n判断：空后是名词短语 bad weather，due to 表示“由于”。\n排除：because、since 通常引导原因从句；despite 意为“尽管”，与这里的因果关系不同。\n记法：由于 + 名词：due to。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md 第22题"},{"number":32,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Under no circumstances _____ to tell lies to parents.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"children are allowed"},{"key":"B","text":"are children allowed"},{"key":"C","text":"will children allow"},{"key":"D","text":"children will allow"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：任何情况下都不允许孩子对父母说谎。\n判断：Under no circumstances 是否定短语，置于句首引起部分倒装；孩子被允许，用 are children allowed。\n排除：children are allowed 没倒装；will children allow 变成孩子允许别人，语态和含义都变了。\n记法：否定短语放句首，助动词移到主语前。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md 第21题"},{"number":33,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Hua Luogeng was a _____ mathematician.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"previous"},{"key":"B","text":"proper"},{"key":"C","text":"prevailing"},{"key":"D","text":"prominent"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：华罗庚是一位杰出的数学家。\n判断：prominent 在这里表示杰出、有声望。\n排除：previous 以前的，proper 适当的，prevailing 流行或占优势的。\n记法：杰出显著：prominent。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第6题"},{"number":34,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"You can go out, _____ you promise to be back before 12 o'clock.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so far as"},{"key":"B","text":"as far as"},{"key":"C","text":"as long as"},{"key":"D","text":"as soon as"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：只要承诺十二点前回来，你就可以出去。\n判断：能出去的条件是承诺按时回来，因此用 as long as，意思是“只要”。\n排除：as soon as 是“一……就……”；so far as / as far as 多表示范围或程度。\n记法：只要条件成立：as long as。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第2题"},{"number":35,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Old and young people learn from each other and _____ each other.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"encourage"},{"key":"B","text":"enhance"},{"key":"C","text":"endeavor"},{"key":"D","text":"encounter"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：年长者和年轻人互相学习，互相鼓励。\n判断：encourage each other 与 learn from each other 在意思上相配。\n排除：enhance 提高；endeavor 努力；encounter 遇到。不要只凭 en 开头猜词。\n记法：给人鼓励：encourage。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第14题"},{"number":36,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"If I _____ you, I _____ more attention to English idioms and phrases.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"was; shall pay"},{"key":"B","text":"am; will pay"},{"key":"C","text":"would be; would pay"},{"key":"D","text":"were; would pay"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：如果我是你，我会更注意英语习语和短语。\n判断：If I were you 是提出假设性建议的常用结构；主句用 would pay。\n排除：现实中“我”不是“你”，不是普通将来条件句。这里不要选 am / will。\n记法：如果我是你：If I were you, I would ...。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md 第19题"},{"number":37,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"Communication plays an important role in a _____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"negotiation"},{"key":"B","text":"irrigation"},{"key":"C","text":"immigration"},{"key":"D","text":"reputation"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：沟通在谈判中起重要作用。\n判断：negotiation 表示谈判，符合 communication 的职场语境。\n排除：irrigation 灌溉，immigration 移民，reputation 声誉。\n记法：协商谈判：negotiation。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md 第11题"},{"number":38,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"—Why didn't you buy a new car? —I would have bought one if I _____ enough money.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"had"},{"key":"B","text":"have had"},{"key":"C","text":"would have"},{"key":"D","text":"had had"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：过去没买新车，是因为当时钱不够。\n判断：问句 did not buy 和主句 would have bought 已确定过去的反事实情景，if 从句用 had had。\n排除：两个 had 不重复：前一个帮助构成过去完成时，后一个是“有”的过去分词。\n记法：过去没做到：if had done，主句 would have done。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md 第26题"},{"number":39,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The new machine is more _____ than the old one, for it can do the same job in half the time.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"effective"},{"key":"B","text":"sufficient"},{"key":"C","text":"significant"},{"key":"D","text":"efficient"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：新机器只用一半时间就能完成同样的工作。\n判断：同样的工作花更少时间，重点是效率高，因此选 efficient。\n排除：effective 强调是否有效、能否达成目的；sufficient 足够的；significant 重要的。\n记法：同样产出省时间：efficient。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第二十一天.md 第29题"},{"number":40,"section":1,"points":1,"stem":"The law requires that everyone _____ his car checked at least once a year.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has"},{"key":"B","text":"had"},{"key":"C","text":"have"},{"key":"D","text":"will have"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：法律要求每个人至少一年检修一次汽车。\n判断：requires 表示要求，后面的从句使用 (should) have；省去 should 后仍用原形 have。\n排除：这里不能按 everyone 是单数就机械选 has；先判断 require 表要求的从句结构。\n记法：要求、建议：从句常用 (should) + 原形。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十一天.md 第26题"},{"number":41,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What is the writer mainly trying to help parents do?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Make their children grow up faster."},{"key":"B","text":"Avoid all disagreements with their children."},{"key":"C","text":"Reduce yelling and communicate more effectively."},{"key":"D","text":"Give older children more responsibilities."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：作者主要想帮助父母做什么？\n判断：第1段点出 reduce the yelling，后面依次给出倾听、合理期望、放低声音等做法。C能概括全文。\n排除：B的 all 过于绝对，文章没有说要消除全部争执；A、D都不是全文目的。\n记法：主旨要覆盖全文，不能只抓一个细节。\n原文依据：here are some ways that can help you reduce the yelling","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R1","passageId":"r1"},{"number":42,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"According to paragraph 2, what may make children more willing to listen?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Parents listening to them first."},{"key":"B","text":"Parents ending the discussion immediately."},{"key":"C","text":"Parents repeating an order more loudly."},{"key":"D","text":"Parents asking another child to explain."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：怎样可能让孩子更愿意倾听？\n判断：第2段末句明确说，如果父母倾听孩子，孩子更可能倾听父母。\n排除：B、C、D都不是原文给出的办法；C还与减少吼叫的主题相反。\n记法：题干有 listen，回到同词附近找条件。\n原文依据：Kids are more likely to listen to you if you listen to them!","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R1","passageId":"r1"},{"number":43,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Why does the writer compare the youngest child with the oldest?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"To show that younger children learn faster."},{"key":"B","text":"To suggest that older children need no guidance."},{"key":"C","text":"To explain why children should share the same tasks."},{"key":"D","text":"To show that expectations should suit a child’s age."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：作者为什么比较最小和最大的孩子？\n判断：第3段说不能要求最小的孩子和最大的孩子同样负责，随后提到考虑年龄，所以期望应符合年龄。\n排除：这段不是比较学习速度，也没说年长孩子不需要指导。\n记法：推断紧跟前后句，不凭生活常识补结论。\n原文依据：You can't expect that your youngest acts as responsibly as your oldest.","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R1","passageId":"r1"},{"number":44,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"The word “whisper” in paragraph 4 is closest in meaning to ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"speak angrily"},{"key":"B","text":"speak very quietly"},{"key":"C","text":"stop speaking completely"},{"key":"D","text":"repeat the same words"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：whisper 最接近什么含义？\n判断：前有 Instead of yelling（代替吼叫），后有 quieter, not louder（更安静而不是更响），可以判断是轻声说话。\n排除：安静地说不等于完全不说，也不是生气地说。\n记法：猜词找反义对照：yell ↔ whisper。\n原文依据：Instead of yelling, you'd better whisper.","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R1","passageId":"r1"},{"number":45,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does the final paragraph suggest when children do not listen?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Assume they are trying to upset their parents."},{"key":"B","text":"Stop giving them any guidance."},{"key":"C","text":"Remember that they are still learning."},{"key":"D","text":"Expect them to behave perfectly next time."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：孩子不听话时，最后一段建议父母怎样想？\n判断：最后一段提醒：孩子仍在学习，不会完美，所以不要立即把事情当成在针对自己。\n排除：A违背 don’t take it personally；D违背 not going to be perfect；B没有依据。\n记法：建议题检查否定词，别把作者反对的做法选进去。\n原文依据：your kids are still learning and they're not going to be perfect","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R1","passageId":"r1"},{"number":46,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What problem led the team leader to arrange the balloon activity?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The cafeteria did not have enough chairs."},{"key":"B","text":"Team members were unwilling to share information."},{"key":"C","text":"The employees did not know one another’s names."},{"key":"D","text":"The team had too few people to finish its work."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：领导为什么组织气球活动？\n判断：第1段明确说员工不愿分享信息或解决办法，过于关注自己，所以领导安排活动。\n排除：桌椅被收起来是布置活动的结果；文章没说人数不足，也没说不认识同事。\n记法：why 问原因，先找问题，再看 as a result 后的行动。\n原文依据：they wouldn't share information or solutions with each other","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R2","passageId":"r2"},{"number":47,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What happened after the team searched for their own balloons for 15 minutes?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"About 30 people had found theirs."},{"key":"B","text":"Everyone had found a balloon without a name."},{"key":"C","text":"The team repeated the balloon-writing task."},{"key":"D","text":"No one had found their own balloon."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：寻找自己名字的气球十五分钟后，结果怎样？\n判断：第3段说 no one had found their balloon。约30人指之前成功写上名字的人，不是此时找到气球的人。\n排除：本题容易把“写上名字”的30人与“找到气球”的人数混淆。\n记法：先锁定活动阶段，再看数字。\n原文依据：After 15 minutes of searching, no one had found their balloon","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R2","passageId":"r2"},{"number":48,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What was different about the third round?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Members passed balloons to the people named on them."},{"key":"B","text":"Members worked alone for a longer time."},{"key":"C","text":"Only team leaders were allowed to search."},{"key":"D","text":"Members had to write new names on the balloons."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：第三轮与前一轮相比有什么变化？\n判断：第4段要求找到任何有名字的气球后，就把它交给对应的人，从各找各的变成互相帮助。\n排除：并不是增加独自搜索时间、只让领导找或重新写名字。\n记法：对比题抓规则改变，不只记最终耗时。\n原文依据：give that balloon to the person whose name was on it","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R2","passageId":"r2"},{"number":49,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"In paragraph 5, “obstacles” most nearly means ______.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"personal rewards"},{"key":"B","text":"shared ambitions"},{"key":"C","text":"difficulties that block progress"},{"key":"D","text":"plans for future activities"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：obstacles 最接近什么意思？\n判断：上文展示合作让团队更有效率，本句却说只盯着个人追求会 create obstacles，因此是制造阻碍。\n排除：rewards 奖励、ambitions 志向、plans 计划都不能表达阻碍合作的负面作用。\n记法：看词的作用：阻挡进展的是障碍。\n原文依据：create obstacles by focusing solely on their own pursuits and goals","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R2","passageId":"r2"},{"number":50,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Which statement best expresses the lesson of the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Individual speed matters more than teamwork."},{"key":"B","text":"Sharing and cooperation can improve team efficiency."},{"key":"C","text":"A team should avoid activities involving games."},{"key":"D","text":"Personal goals should never be discussed at work."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：整篇文章最主要的启示是什么？\n判断：活动从十五分钟无人找到，到互相帮助后两分钟人人找到，领导据此总结分享与合作提高效率。\n排除：D把关注团队扩大成“永远不能谈个人目标”，超出文章；A与实验结果相反。\n记法：故事主旨：看结果变化，再找作者总结。\n原文依据：much better at problem solving when we are working together, not individually","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R2","passageId":"r2"},{"number":51,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does Macharia’s tracking device mainly help car owners do?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Pay for repairs through their phones."},{"key":"B","text":"Reduce the fuel their vehicles use."},{"key":"C","text":"Learn to drive safely on busy roads."},{"key":"D","text":"Locate their cars and find them if stolen."}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：这套追踪装置主要帮助车主做什么？\n判断：第2段直接说明：知道汽车在哪里，并在汽车被盗后找到它。\n排除：维修付款、节油和驾驶培训都没有在装置功能中出现。\n记法：功能题定位 help ... do，不把一般科技用途套进去。\n原文依据：help owners know where their cars are, and find them if they are stolen","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R3","passageId":"r3"},{"number":52,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"How can an owner stop a stolen car from moving, according to the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By sending it a command in a text message."},{"key":"B","text":"By calling the factory that made the device."},{"key":"C","text":"By removing the tracker from the vehicle."},{"key":"D","text":"By switching off the owner’s computer."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：车主通过什么方式让被盗车辆停止移动？\n判断：第3段说车主通过短信向车辆发送指令信号，随后车辆停止移动。\n排除：不是打电话给工厂，也不是拿掉追踪器；文中没有说关闭电脑会使车辆停车。\n记法：过程题顺着“动作 → 结果”找。\n原文依据：send a command signal to the vehicle through a text message","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R3","passageId":"r3"},{"number":53,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What did Macharia do after he was satisfied with his first device’s design?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"He stopped using locally available materials forever."},{"key":"B","text":"He sold his company to a Chinese buyer."},{"key":"C","text":"He arranged for a factory in China to manufacture the device."},{"key":"D","text":"He decided to use the device only in his own vehicles."}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：对最初设备的设计满意后，他做了什么？\n判断：第4段说他把制造工作外包给中国工厂。这里是制造安排，不是出售公司。\n排除：A的 forever、D的 only 都是原文没有给出的限制；B把生产外包误读成公司出售。\n记法：after / when 后先找时间节点，再找紧随其后的行动。\n原文依据：he outsourced the making of the device to a factory in China","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R3","passageId":"r3"},{"number":54,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"What does Tony Wanga’s experience show about the trackers?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They can replace drivers on all his vehicles."},{"key":"B","text":"They allow him to monitor his vehicles from his office."},{"key":"C","text":"They cost $250 in total for all three vehicles."},{"key":"D","text":"They work only when the owner is inside the car."}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：客户Tony Wanga的经历说明追踪器有什么用途？\n判断：第4段末尾说，他坐在办公室就能跟踪车辆行程，支持远程监控这一用途。\n排除：$250是每台价格，不是三台总价；追踪器不代替司机，也不要求车主坐在车内。\n记法：实例题抓实例证实的功能；数字注意 each。\n原文依据：he can follow its travels as he sits in his office","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R3","passageId":"r3"},{"number":55,"section":2,"points":2,"stem":"Which description best fits Macharia’s work in the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"He applies technology to practical security problems."},{"key":"B","text":"He focuses mainly on building faster vehicles."},{"key":"C","text":"He develops devices only for government use."},{"key":"D","text":"He has stopped improving products since his first invention."}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：哪一项最能概括Macharia的工作？\n判断：汽车定位、防盗报警、笔内摄像头、无线安防摄像头，都在利用技术解决实际安全问题。\n排除：文中没有制造更快汽车或只服务政府；最后一段明确说他继续开发产品。\n记法：人物工作概括：把多项产品归到共同用途。\n原文依据：continues to develop other security products","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"R3","passageId":"r3"},{"number":56,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第56空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"direction"},{"key":"B","text":"invention"},{"key":"C","text":"attention"},{"key":"D","text":"competition"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：顾客是被关注的中心。\n判断：center of attention 是关注焦点，和下一句让顾客感到特别相呼应。\n排除：direction 方向、invention 发明、competition 竞争都不合语境。\n记法：关注的中心：center of attention。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":57,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第57空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"feel"},{"key":"B","text":"feeling"},{"key":"C","text":"felt"},{"key":"D","text":"to feel"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：优质服务让顾客觉得自己很特别。\n判断：make somebody do something；这里 making 后仍使用 feel 原形。\n排除：不是看到 making 就让后面的动词也变成 doing。\n记法：使役 make + 人 + 动词原形。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":58,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第58空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"watched"},{"key":"B","text":"watch"},{"key":"C","text":"to watching"},{"key":"D","text":"watching"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：顾客通常看不到店员闲坐着看电视或打牌。\n判断：sitting around 后面的 watching 和 playing 并列，补充店员同时在做什么。\n排除：playing cards 已给出平行结构线索；不要把动词随意改成过去式。\n记法：并列看同伴：watching ... or playing ...。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":59,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第59空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Otherwise"},{"key":"B","text":"Instead"},{"key":"C","text":"Therefore"},{"key":"D","text":"Meanwhile"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：店员不是闲坐娱乐，而是热情招呼顾客。\n判断：前一句否定不良服务，后一句说实际做法，用 Instead 表示“相反”。\n排除：Therefore 表结果；Otherwise 表否则；Meanwhile 表同时，不如 Instead 准确表达替代关系。\n记法：前面不是这样，后面改说那样：Instead。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":60,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第60空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"that"},{"key":"B","text":"which"},{"key":"C","text":"what"},{"key":"D","text":"where"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：店员帮助顾客找到他们想要的东西。\n判断：what they want 既作 find 的宾语，what 又在从句里作 want 的宾语，表示“所想要的东西”。\n排除：that 在从句中不承担宾语；where 表地点；这里没有给 which 一个明确的选择范围。\n记法：缺“所……的东西”，考虑 what。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":61,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第61空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"since"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"although"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：顾客一般不必问价，因为标价清楚。\n判断：标价清楚是不必询价的原因，since 在这里表示因为。\n排除：unless 除非、although 尽管、until 直到，都不表达这里的因果。\n记法：先读两边意思，再选连接词。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":62,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第62空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"similar"},{"key":"B","text":"absent"},{"key":"C","text":"afraid"},{"key":"D","text":"ready"}],"answer":"D","explanation":"题意：顾客准备结账时，可以去收银通道。\n判断：be ready to do 表示准备好做某事。\n排除：similar 通常接 to + 名词；absent 缺席的；afraid 害怕的，与结账流程不合。\n记法：准备做某事：be ready to do。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":63,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第63空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"invitations"},{"key":"B","text":"purchases"},{"key":"C","text":"complaints"},{"key":"D","text":"directions"}],"answer":"B","explanation":"题意：付完所购商品的钱后，顾客收到店员的感谢。\n判断：purchases 指购买的东西，与 pay for、checkout 都属于购物语境。\n排除：complaints 是投诉，directions 是指示或方向，invitations 是邀请。\n记法：结账付的是所购物品：purchases。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":64,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第64空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"enjoy"},{"key":"B","text":"practise"},{"key":"C","text":"avoid"},{"key":"D","text":"finish"}],"answer":"C","explanation":"题意：服务差，顾客今后可能避免在这家店购物。\n判断：poor service 给出负面体验，avoid shopping 表示避免继续在此购物。\n排除：四个词后面都可能接 doing，单看语法不够，必须结合服务差的语境。\n记法：语法都通时，用上下文定词义。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":65,"section":3,"points":1,"stem":"第65空（请结合短文作答）","options":[{"key":"A","text":"even if"},{"key":"B","text":"so that"},{"key":"C","text":"as soon as"},{"key":"D","text":"in case"}],"answer":"A","explanation":"题意：服务好的商家，即使价格更高，也能留住顾客。\n判断：价格高通常是不利因素，却仍然忠诚，形成让步，用 even if。\n排除：so that 表目的或结果；as soon as 表时间；in case 表以防。\n记法：即使有不利条件，结果照样成立：even if。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"C1","passageId":"cloze"},{"number":66,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Besides, the more time you spend with your kids, the better you'll get at communicating with them.","options":[],"answer":"除此之外，你陪伴孩子的时间越长，你就越能更好地和他们沟通。","explanation":"题意：父母陪伴孩子越多，越善于与他们沟通。\n判断：把 the more ..., the better ... 合起来译成“越……，就越……”。spend time with 是陪伴，get better at 是更擅长。\n排除：不要只译成“更多、更好”而丢掉两者随之变化的关系。\n记法：先找比较框架，再补具体动作。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第四天.md 第29题"},{"number":67,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"Kelvin Macharia has invented a tracking device that uses computers and wireless technology to help owners know where their cars are.","options":[],"answer":"开尔文·马查里亚发明了一种追踪装置，它利用电脑和无线技术让车主知道车的位置。","explanation":"题意：追踪装置利用电脑和无线技术，帮助车主了解车辆位置。\n判断：主干是 Kelvin Macharia has invented a tracking device；that 后说明装置功能；where their cars are 表示车辆的位置。\n排除：that 修饰 device，不是修饰发明者；where 后是陈述语序。\n记法：长句分三层：谁做了什么 → 什么样的装置 → 帮助知道什么。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md 第26题"},{"number":68,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"You cannot live in the past, so denying that change could occur only makes things more complicated for you.","options":[],"answer":"你不能活在过去，所以否认变化可能发生只会让事情对你来说更加复杂。","explanation":"题意：否认变化会让事情变复杂。\n判断：前句 cannot live in the past；后句主语是一整块 denying that change could occur，谓语是 makes，宾语补足语是 more complicated。\n排除：否定、only 和 more 都要保留；不要把 denying 错当成主句谓语。\n记法：先圈主语整块，再找 makes。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第七天.md 第23题"},{"number":69,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"One's health should never be sacrificed for a need to work hard.","options":[],"answer":"永远不要为了迎合高强度的工作而牺牲个人健康。","explanation":"题意：不应为了高强度工作牺牲个人健康。\n判断：主语是 One’s health；should never be sacrificed 表示绝不应被牺牲；for 后说明原因。\n排除：never 是否定词，不能漏掉；中文可以改为主动表达，让译文通顺。\n记法：先保留否定和情态，再把被动译通顺。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十天.md 第20题"},{"number":70,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"When you motivate people to pool their knowledge, the results may exceed your expectations.","options":[],"answer":"当你激发员工集思广益时，结果可能超出你的预期。","explanation":"题意：激励大家汇集知识，结果可能超出预期。\n判断：when 从句先交代情景；pool their knowledge 指汇集知识或集思广益；may exceed 表示可能超出。\n排除：pool 在这里是动词，不是游泳池；may 表可能，不能翻成一定。\n记法：熟词换词性：pool knowledge = 汇集知识。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md 第13题"},{"number":71,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"这个故事使我想起了我的母亲。","options":[],"answer":"This story reminds me of my mother.","explanation":"题意：这个故事使我想起母亲。\n判断：主语 This story 是单数，谓语用 reminds；使某人想起某事用 remind somebody of something。\n排除：不要写成 remind me my mother 而漏掉 of。\n记法：使某人想起：remind somebody of。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第三天.md 第28题"},{"number":72,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"她花了很长时间读这本书。","options":[],"answer":"It took her a long time to read this book.","explanation":"题意：她花了很长时间读这本书。\n判断：过去发生，用 It took her a long time to read this book。It 作形式主语，to read 说明花时间做的事。\n排除：人称用宾格 her；read 前面的 to 不能省。\n记法：某人花时间做事：It takes somebody time to do。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第五天.md 第18题"},{"number":73,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"他儿子太小不能上学。","options":[],"answer":"His son is too young to go to school.","explanation":"题意：儿子太小，还不能上学。\n判断：用 too young to go to school，把“太……不能……”放进同一个结构。\n排除：不要写成 too young that ...；to 后接动词原形 go。\n记法：太……不能：too + 形容词 + to do。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第八天.md 第22题"},{"number":74,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"当他到达车站时，火车已经开走了。","options":[],"answer":"When he arrived at the station, the train had already left.","explanation":"题意：到车站时，火车已经开走了。\n判断：到车站用一般过去时 arrived；开走发生得更早，用 had already left。\n排除：两个动作不是同时发生；不要都译成现在时。\n记法：过去之前先发生：had done。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第十二天.md 第3题"},{"number":75,"section":4,"points":2,"stem":"这部电影值得一看。","options":[],"answer":"The film is worth seeing.","explanation":"题意：这部电影值得看。\n判断：be worth doing 表示值得做某事；The film is worth seeing。\n排除：不能写 worth to see；这种结构通常用主动的 doing 表被动含义。\n记法：值得做：be worth doing。","reviewRequired":false,"notes":[],"source":"英语刷题打卡第六天.md 第18题"}],"passages":[{"id":"r1","title":"Stop Yelling at Your Kids","paragraphs":["Parenting is hard. If you're a parent, I'm sure that I don't need to tell you that our job is a tough one. When you're managing children, it can be difficult to remember that they are still learning. If you find that you are yelling at your kids more often than you want to, here are some ways that can help you reduce the yelling. I've been working on this for the past few months and I have to say, it's been amazing for both the kids and me.","If you are having an argument with your child, you need to make sure you both take the time to really listen. It gives both of you time to think and really listen to each other, which is important. Kids are more likely to listen to you if you listen to them!","One of your biggest struggles is to remind yourself of appropriate expectations. You can't expect that your youngest acts as responsibly as your oldest. You should lower what you expect — taking into consideration things like their age — it can make a big difference.","You should do your best to take a moment before yelling and take in a deep breath. It makes a world of difference for you. Instead of yelling, you'd better whisper. It can also help defuse any situation by making things quieter, not louder. Besides, the more time you spend with your kids, the better you'll get at communicating with them. You're both more likely to understand each other.","If your children aren't listening or it seems they only don't listen to you, don't take it personally. You should remind yourself that your kids are still learning and they're not going to be perfect."],"questionNumbers":[41,42,43,44,45]},{"id":"r2","title":"A Teamwork Game","paragraphs":["A team of about 35 employees had come together for a team building event. They were a young, bright and enthusiastic team. However, one of their chief problems was the fact that they wouldn't share information or solutions with each other, and the team leader thought they were too focused on themselves and not on the team. As a result, she brought them all into the cafeteria. All of the tables and chairs had been stored away, and fun decorations and hundreds of different colored balloons had been placed around the room.","In the center of the room was a big box of balloons that hadn't been blown up yet.","The team leader instructed everybody to pick a balloon, blow it up, and write their name on it, but they had to be careful not to burst the balloon. Although they were given a second chance if their first balloon popped , they were out of the game the second time round. In the end, about 30 team members wrote their names without their balloons popping. They were then asked to leave the room and, after five minutes, the team leader brought them back in and asked them to find the balloon with their name on it amongst the hundreds of other balloons in the room. After 15 minutes of searching, no one had found their balloon, and the team were told that they were then going to move on to the third round of the activity.","In this round, each team member was instructed to find any balloon with a name on it and then give that balloon to the person whose name was on it. Within two minutes, everybody had their own balloon. The team leader summarized the activity thus: “We are much more efficient when we are willing to share with each other and much better at problem solving when we are working together, not individually.”","Sometimes, members of teams create obstacles by focusing solely on their own pursuits and goals.","Every member of the team should ask themselves on a regular basis what they are doing and what they can do for the team."],"questionNumbers":[46,47,48,49,50]},{"id":"r3","title":"Young Technology Expert Works to Stop Car Thefts","paragraphs":["Kenya has East Africa's largest economy. Its capital city is growing quickly, but so is the city's crime rate. Thieves in the capital steal an average of 10 cars each day.","Kelvin Macharia has invented a tracking device that uses computers and wireless technology to help owners know where their cars are, and find them if they are stolen. Mr. Macharia is just 24 years old. He is the CEO of Sunrise Tracking.","He began working on his invention in 2012. Using $300 from his savings, he improved a system that was already being used to find stolen cars. His smart anti-theft system uses a computer or a mobile phone to tell owners where their cars are. Mr. Macharia says if a car is stolen, the owner can find it using his tracking device. The owner is able to send a command signal to the vehicle through a text message. It immediately stops the car from moving. Experts say this shows the power of security solutions that involve mobile technology.","Mr. Macharia used material available in Kenya to make his first tracker device. When he was satisfied with the design, he outsourced the making of the device to a factory in China. He says his company is now worth more than $100,000 and has more than 100 companies as clients. Tony Wanga is one of those clients. He owns three minibus taxis. Car thieves in the capital have targeted these vehicles. Mr. Wanga bought trackers for each of his vehicles. The trackers cost $250 each. He says the trackers tell him where his vehicles are. He says when the tracker is placed in one of his vehicles, he can follow its travels as he sits in his office.","Mr. Macharia continues to develop other security products. His other security products include car alarms and a camera hidden inside a pen. And he says he is building a wireless security camera that will be able to store video information for long periods of time. Mr. Macharia hopes his technological innovations give his clients the security and safety they want and need."],"questionNumbers":[51,52,53,54,55]},{"id":"cloze","title":"Customer Service","paragraphs":["The American idea of customer service is to make each customer the center of [56]. And wherever you go, good customer service means making customers [57] special.","When customers get to a store, they are treated as honored guests. Customers don't usually find store clerks sitting around [58] TV or playing cards. [59], the clerks greet them warmly and offer to help them find [60] they want. Customers usually don't have to ask how much items cost, [61] prices are clearly marked.","When customers are [62] to check out, they can go to the nearest and shortest checkout lane. Good stores open new checkout lanes when the lineups get too long. Some even offer express lanes for customers with 10 items or less. After they pay for their [63], customers receive a smile and a warm \"thank you and have a nice day\" from the clerk.","Customer service in America grows out of the belief that \"the customer is always right\". If a person receives poor service from a store, he probably will [64] shopping there in the future. On the other hand, customers often remain loyal to a business that has excellent service [65] their prices are higher."],"questionNumbers":[56,57,58,59,60,61,62,63,64,65]}],"references":[]}]};
